cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize GlucoShield in academic research, educational material, or clinical decision-support studies, please cite it as below."
title: "GlucoShield: Physics-Informed Neural-ODE Glucose Forecasting & Automated Meal-Aware Clinical Decision-Support Platform"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sanjeeth"
    given-names: "Sai D."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sanjeeth-4AM/GlucoShield"
url: "https://github.com/Sanjeeth-4AM/GlucoShield"
abstract: >-
  GlucoShield is a research-grade hybrid glucose forecasting and clinical decision-support
  architecture combining a multi-task gated recurrent unit (GRU-128) with an 8-compartment
  nonlinear Hovorka ordinary differential equation (ODE) digital twin solved via Runge-Kutta 4.
  The certified production serving engine (Combination C) unifies point forecast trajectories
  from a frozen deep neural model with calibrated regime-conditioned prediction intervals,
  achieving 95.28% Clarke Error Grid Zone A+B clinical accuracy and 96.39% empirical prediction
  interval coverage on external validation cohorts.
keywords:
  - continuous-glucose-monitoring
  - physics-informed-neural-networks
  - neural-ode
  - diabetes-technology
  - multi-horizon-forecasting
  - digital-twin
  - clinical-decision-support
  - time-series
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
